From d0c19c3160754d705e82ad29721dc431bb7fa031 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: im486dx <im486dx@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 19:33:40 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] BK7252N: add BKCam driver (DVP camera, JPEG snapshot and
 MJPEG stream)

New driver for the BK7252N's DVP camera interface and JPEG encoder:

- /snapshot.jpg  newest frame as image/jpeg
- /stream        MJPEG (multipart/x-mixed-replace), for browsers, VLC and
                 Android MJPEG viewers
- /cam           small viewer page; the main page links to it
- commands CamStart, CamStop, CamInfo, CamReg <reg> [value], and CamDump
  (prints a frame as hex on the console UART, for bring-up without Wi-Fi)

The SDK's camera_intf does the hardware part: sensor clock and DVP pins,
sensor init over I2C1, encoder and GDMA. The driver copies the GDMA chunks
of each frame into one of three 48 KB buffers, trims the frame to its EOI
marker, and serves the newest complete frame while capture continues.

Enable it with `startDriver BKCam` (for example as the startup command).

Requires the beken_freertos_sdk change that builds camera_intf on BK7252N
and adds GC0329 support; the sdk/beken_freertos_sdk submodule must be
bumped to it.

Tested on a BK7252N battery camera with a GC0329C sensor: 640x480 at
10 fps, ~9 KB per frame, streamed over Wi-Fi in AP and STA mode.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
